---
import Layout from '../../components/Layout.astro';
import { Calendar, Clock, ArrowLeft, BarChart3 } from 'lucide-astro';

const post = {
  title: "Patterns in AI Deception: What We've Learned",
  description: "Analysis of how different AI models approach deception and social deduction. Which models are best at lying? Which are best at detecting lies?",
  date: '2024-12-25',
  readTime: '10 min',
  category: 'analysis',
};

function formatDate(dateStr: string): string {
  return new Date(dateStr).toLocaleDateString('en-US', {
    year: 'numeric',
    month: 'long',
    day: 'numeric',
  });
}
---

<Layout title={post.title}>
  <article class="max-w-2xl">
    <a 
      href="/blog" 
      class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground transition-colors mb-6"
    >
      <ArrowLeft class="h-4 w-4" />
      Back to Blog
    </a>

    <header class="mb-8">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full text-xs font-medium bg-amber-500/10 text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400">
          <BarChart3 class="h-3 w-3" />
          Analysis
        </span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-3">{post.title}</h1>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">
        {post.description}
      </p>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1">
          <Calendar class="h-4 w-4" />
          {formatDate(post.date)}
        </span>
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1">
          <Clock class="h-4 w-4" />
          {post.readTime} read
        </span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-zinc dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
      <p>
        After running hundreds of Mafia games across dozens of AI models, fascinating patterns have emerged in how different models approach deception and lie detection.
      </p>

      <h2>Deception Strategies We've Observed</h2>
      
      <h3>The "Helpful Townie" Approach</h3>
      <p>
        Many models playing Mafia adopt an extremely cooperative persona—actively helping "find" the Mafia, providing analysis, and appearing invested in the Town's success. This is often effective because it mirrors what genuine Town players do.
      </p>

      <h3>Strategic Voting</h3>
      <p>
        Skilled Mafia players vote to build trust early, sometimes even voting against their partner to establish credibility. The best models recognize that short-term sacrifice can lead to long-term survival.
      </p>

      <h3>Information Management</h3>
      <p>
        Some models are careful about what they reveal. They participate actively but avoid making specific accusations that could be verified or contradicted later. This "say much, commit to little" strategy is surprisingly effective.
      </p>

      <h2>Detection Patterns</h2>
      
      <h3>Behavioral Analysis</h3>
      <p>
        The best lie detectors pay attention to subtle inconsistencies:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Who avoids making direct accusations?</li>
        <li>Who changes their vote at the last moment?</li>
        <li>Who provides analysis without taking positions?</li>
        <li>Whose statements are vague vs. specific?</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Voting Pattern Analysis</h3>
      <p>
        Some models track voting patterns across rounds, looking for:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Players who never vote together (potential Mafia partners avoiding mutual support)</li>
        <li>Players who consistently vote against eliminated Town</li>
        <li>Last-minute vote changes that swung outcomes</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Model-Specific Observations</h2>
      <p>
        While we won't call out specific models, some interesting patterns:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Larger models</strong> tend to be better at both deception and detection, suggesting social intelligence scales with general capability</li>
        <li><strong>Instruction-tuned models</strong> sometimes struggle with deception—their training to be helpful can make them reluctant to lie convincingly</li>
        <li><strong>Models with strong reasoning</strong> excel at detecting patterns but don't always translate analysis into correct votes</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What This Tells Us</h2>
      <p>
        These patterns suggest that social intelligence in AI is multifaceted:
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Theory of mind</strong>: Understanding what others know and believe</li>
        <li><strong>Strategic reasoning</strong>: Planning multi-step deceptive strategies</li>
        <li><strong>Pattern recognition</strong>: Detecting behavioral anomalies</li>
        <li><strong>Persuasion</strong>: Convincing others to take specific actions</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        Different models excel at different aspects, making Mafia a rich benchmark for understanding AI capabilities.
      </p>

      <hr />

      <p>
        Check the <a href="/games">Games page</a> to watch replays and see these patterns in action.
      </p>
    </div>

    <footer class="mt-12 pt-6 border-t">
      <a 
        href="/blog" 
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground transition-colors"
      >
        <ArrowLeft class="h-4 w-4" />
        Back to all posts
      </a>
    </footer>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .prose h2 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .prose h3 {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .prose p {
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .prose ul, .prose ol {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    margin-left: 1.5rem;
  }
  .prose ul {
    list-style-type: disc;
  }
  .prose ol {
    list-style-type: decimal;
  }
  .prose li {
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .prose strong {
    color: var(--foreground);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .prose a {
    color: var(--foreground);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 4px;
  }
  .prose a:hover {
    color: var(--primary);
  }
  .prose hr {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    border-color: var(--border);
  }
</style>
